---
import LegalPage from "../components/site/LegalPage.astro";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Refunds & Cancellations"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  updated="30 August 2026"
>
  <h2>Membership fees</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Membership fees are generally non-refundable once the period has begun.
    </li>
    <li>If you were charged in error, or charged twice, we refund in full.</li>
    <li>
      If the club cannot provide court access for a sustained period, we refund
      pro rata or extend your membership by the same period, at your choice.
    </li>
    <li>
      Requests on medical grounds are considered case by case — write to
      [contact email] with supporting details.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Court bookings</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Cancel a booking any time from your dashboard at no charge.</li>
    <li>
      Where a court is charged separately and the club cancels, that charge is
      refunded in full.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tournament entry fees</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Refundable in full if you withdraw before the registration deadline.
    </li>
    <li>
      After the deadline, entry fees are usually not refundable, since the club
      has already paid the organiser.
    </li>
    <li>
      If an event is cancelled by the organiser, we pass on whatever they
      refund.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How refunds are made</h2>
  <p>
    Approved refunds go back to the original payment method through Razorpay.
    They are typically initiated within 5 working days of approval, and your
    bank or card issuer may take a further 5–7 working days to credit them.
  </p>

  <h2>Requesting a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Email [contact email] with your registered mobile number, the payment
    reference from your dashboard, and the reason. We respond within 5 working
    days.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
